# asterisk — PBX server CLI

## Connect to a running Asterisk session

```sh
asterisk -rvvv
```

## Issue a command from the shell

```sh
asterisk -rx "<command>"
```

## Originate an echo call from a SIP trunk to a number

```sh
asterisk -rx "channel originate SIP/<trunk>/<number> application echo"
```

## Inspect SIP accounts

```sh
# Details of SIP accounts
asterisk -rx "sip show peers"

# Passwords of SIP accounts
asterisk -rx "sip show users"
```

## Current active channels

```sh
asterisk -rx "core show channels"
```

## Real-world: health check from a monitoring script

```sh
if asterisk -rx "core show uptime" | grep -q "System uptime"; then
    echo "asterisk OK"
else
    systemctl restart asterisk
fi
```

## Real-world: reload dialplan after editing extensions.conf

```sh
asterisk -rx "dialplan reload"
```

| Flag  | What it does                       |
| ----- | ---------------------------------- |
| -r    | attach to running instance         |
| -v    | add verbosity (stackable: -rvvv)   |
| -x    | run one CLI command and exit       |
